.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SMIME_WRITE_PKCS7 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SMIME_write_PKCS7
.Nd convert PKCS#7 structure to S/MIME format
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs7.h
.Ft int
.Fo SMIME_write_PKCS7
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "PKCS7 *p7"
.Fa "BIO *data"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SMIME_write_PKCS7
adds the appropriate MIME headers to a PKCS#7 structure to produce an
S/MIME message.
.Pp
.Fa out
is the BIO to write the data to.
.Fa p7
is the appropriate
.Vt PKCS7
structure.
If streaming is enabled then the content must be supplied in the
.Fa data
argument.
.Fa flags
is an optional set of flags.
.Sh NOTES
The following flags can be passed in the
.Fa flags
parameter.
.Pp
If
.Sy PKCS7_DETACHED
is set then cleartext signing will be used, this option only makes sense
for signedData where
.Sy PKCS7_DETACHED
is also set when
.Xr PKCS7_sign 3
is also called.
.Pp
If the
.Sy PKCS7_TEXT
flag is set MIME headers for type
.Sy text/plain
are added to the content, this only makes sense if
.Sy PKCS7_DETACHED
is also set.
.Pp
If the
.Sy PKCS7_STREAM
flag is set streaming is performed.
This flag should only be set if
.Sy PKCS7_STREAM
was also set in the previous call to
.Xr PKCS7_sign 3
or
.Xr PKCS7_encrypt 3 .
.Pp
If cleartext signing is being used and
.Sy PKCS7_STREAM
not set then the data must be read twice: once to compute the signature
in
.Xr PKCS7_sign 3
and once to output the S/MIME message.
.Pp
If streaming is performed the content is output in BER format using
indefinite length constructed encoding except in the case of signed data
with detached content where the content is absent and DER format is
used.
.Sh BUGS
.Fn SMIME_write_PKCS7
always base64 encodes PKCS#7 structures, there should be an option to
disable this.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SMIME_write_PKCS7
returns 1 for success or 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr PKCS7_sign 3 ,
.Xr PKCS7_verify 3 ,
.Xr PKCS7_encrypt 3
.Xr PKCS7_decrypt 3
